---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { execSync } from 'node:child_process';

let revision = 'local';
try { revision = execSync('git rev-parse --short HEAD').toString().trim(); } catch {}
const builtOn = new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric' });
---
<Base title="How this site is built · Aditya Singh" description="No JavaScript: how this portfolio works." path="/colophon/">
  <section class="section wrap first" aria-labelledby="c-title">
    <p class="kicker">This site</p>
    <h1 class="h2" id="c-title">How this site is built.</h1>
    <div class="colophon">
      <div><b>No JavaScript</b><p>Not one line. It is HTML and CSS, and its security policy forbids scripts outright.</p><code>script-src 'none'</code></div>
      <div><b>The motion</b><p>Drawings play as they scroll into view. With reduced motion on, or in a browser without support, you get the finished layout.</p><code>animation-timeline: view()</code></div>
      <div><b>The 3D stack</b><p>Five slabs in CSS 3D, pulled apart by an animation on the scroll position.</p><code>transform-style: preserve-3d</code></div>
      <div><b>The timeline</b><p>Counted from git logs across 34 repos when the site is built, then frozen into plain SVG.</p><code>git log --since=2026-07-01</code></div>
      <div><b>The type</b><p>Anek, from Ek Type in India, wide for headings and normal for reading. IBM Plex Mono for dates and code.</p><code>font-stretch: 120%</code></div>
      <div><b>This build</b><p>Built on {builtOn} from revision {revision}. Right-click and view source: it is all there.</p><code>0 KB of JavaScript</code></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
